{"agent":"fx-glob-waits","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`_clash_text` returns after the first live lease whose final pairs are non-empty, so the `keep` list is computed only from that first lease. With two live leases that clash on different requested globs (e.g. requested `[\"a.txt\", \"b.txt\"]`; holder X clashes only on `a.txt` and changed paths overlap `a.txt`, holder Y clashes only on `b.txt`), the function returns `keep=[\"b.txt\"]` and the user-facing message says `b.txt would be accepted`. That is wrong: `_clash_text` never checked Y, so `b.txt` would be refused separately.","digest":"a5799be90d2aed8a","location":"ddflow/services/leases.py:_clash_text","severity":"LOW","title":"ddflow/services/leases.py:_clash_text"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"The assertion `assert \"for 0 min\" in text` is time-dependent. `_setup` claims H1 and the test immediately checks that the refusal says the lease has been held for exactly `0 min`. In a slow or paused environment where more than 60 seconds elapse between the claim and the `run_cli(repo, \"update\", ...)` invocation, the holder age will be `for 1 min` (or more), causing this test to fail spuriously even when the fix is correct.","digest":"126a154cdcb05858","location":"tests/test_glob_update_overlap.py:39","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_glob_update_overlap.py:39"}],"chunks_total":2,"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":7531,"diff_sha":"a36b03feb68051abee4deb2c979fc9a4b0587e3e69084a926d521ffa836d264d","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":705.3,"family":"deepseek","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","output_digest":"43b218e279e60d2c","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B-shared-glob-update-waits.rubber_duck.lan-deepseek-v4-pro.20261021T173113Z-5c0f1